1
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:43,970
He's fast!

2
00:01:47,790 --> 00:01:50,090
Faster than anyone I've fought before.

3
00:02:04,060 --> 00:02:06,520
And that sword...

4
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:09,710
He uses the curve of the blade.

5
00:02:09,710 --> 00:02:12,210
He's handling a dagger's range well, too.

6
00:02:14,310 --> 00:02:17,490
Are you serious? He's unarmed.

7
00:02:18,630 --> 00:02:21,480
I'm a warrior of Miklagard.

8
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:29,380
He hasn't experienced
a single good thing, huh?

9
00:02:27,290 --> 00:02:32,290
The Road Home

10
00:02:31,150 --> 00:02:32,360
No kidding.

11
00:02:32,770 --> 00:02:37,010
What kind of monsters surrounded him?

12
00:02:52,190 --> 00:02:53,770
I'll overwhelm him with a flurry of blows.

13
00:02:58,530 --> 00:03:00,020
Dodge this!

14
00:03:15,270 --> 00:03:16,420
He's strong.

15
00:03:18,260 --> 00:03:22,280
What's a warrior this skilled doing
defending a farm?

16
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:26,290
How'd a man this skilled end up a slave?

17
00:03:27,710 --> 00:03:30,040
No, don't get worked up.

18
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:32,470
Don't follow his lead.

19
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:35,410
The important thing is...

20
00:03:47,710 --> 00:03:49,320
He can strike even faster?

21
00:03:51,110 --> 00:03:52,080
But...

22
00:03:53,940 --> 00:03:54,980
I see it.

23
00:04:10,450 --> 00:04:11,880
He got me.

24
00:04:13,230 --> 00:04:14,790
He's next to Gardar...

25
00:04:37,390 --> 00:04:37,990
Snake!

26
00:04:37,990 --> 00:04:39,170
Please don't, Mister Snake!

27
00:04:43,430 --> 00:04:47,460
Please don't kill Gardar.

28
00:04:49,430 --> 00:04:53,090
Please let this go.

29
00:05:00,950 --> 00:05:04,330
Don't be so self-centered, Arnheid.

30
00:05:05,470 --> 00:05:08,870
He killed five of my men.

31
00:05:08,870 --> 00:05:10,650
I can't overlook that.

32
00:05:11,580 --> 00:05:18,200
Snake! I'll do whatever I can to express
my condolences for the loss of your men.

33
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:20,140
I'll even sell my farm to—

34
00:05:20,140 --> 00:05:23,480
Shut up, Gramps! This isn't about money!

35
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:33,600
Both me and my men are a
bunch of stupid, nasty scumbags.

36
00:05:34,070 --> 00:05:39,600
We're drifters who can't use our real names
because of what we've done elsewhere.

37
00:05:40,010 --> 00:05:43,590
But does that mean
it doesn't matter if we die, huh?

38
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:47,790
Is Gardar's life worth that much?

39
00:05:47,790 --> 00:05:49,990
More than the lives of five of my men?

40
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:53,990
Tell me, Thorfinn! Arnheid!

41
00:05:54,470 --> 00:05:56,770
Tell me how much more he's worth.

42
00:06:06,690 --> 00:06:09,850
They're not that different, huh?

43
00:06:11,270 --> 00:06:12,640
In that case...

44
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:13,450
Don't—

45
00:06:14,110 --> 00:06:16,170
The cost of life...

46
00:06:16,890 --> 00:06:19,890
...can only be paid with life!

47
00:07:05,310 --> 00:07:07,000
You still want to fight?

48
00:07:08,900 --> 00:07:12,580
Will you avenge Gardar?

49
00:07:17,630 --> 00:07:21,430
Arnheid, you're the one who
cut Gardar's bonds, aren't you?

50
00:07:23,350 --> 00:07:26,410
You two will be punished accordingly.

51
00:07:27,630 --> 00:07:30,630
Until the master returns, you'll be bound—

52
00:08:00,950 --> 00:08:03,790
Enough, Gardar!

53
00:08:07,490 --> 00:08:09,800
If you keep choking him, he'll die!

54
00:08:10,290 --> 00:08:11,800
Gardar!

55
00:08:12,190 --> 00:08:14,500
Damn! He's so strong...

56
00:08:19,890 --> 00:08:21,270
Gardar!

57
00:08:24,310 --> 00:08:25,690
Let go!

58
00:08:28,190 --> 00:08:29,560
Gardar!

59
00:08:40,470 --> 00:08:41,650
Gardar.

60
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:46,760
Let's go home, Gardar.

61
00:08:55,490 --> 00:08:57,250
That's enough.

62
00:08:58,290 --> 00:09:02,100
There's no one to get in our way anymore.

63
00:09:03,030 --> 00:09:05,510
Hjalti is waiting for us.

64
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:33,530
Hjalti...

65
00:09:36,740 --> 00:09:41,850
Where is he now?

66
00:09:56,580 --> 00:10:00,810
He's with your brother in Birka.

67
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:04,710
I sent him to safety
before the fighting started.

68
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:12,630
I see. My brother's always
done so much for me.

69
00:10:13,300 --> 00:10:18,870
I'll need to bring something to thank him
when we go to get Hjalti.

70
00:10:21,830 --> 00:10:24,360
You there...

71
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:29,090
Is this your cart?

72
00:10:29,690 --> 00:10:31,240
I'd like to borrow it.

73
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:33,000
Uh, actually...

74
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:35,360
It's mine.

75
00:10:36,560 --> 00:10:40,250
You can have it, Gardar.

76
00:10:41,310 --> 00:10:42,360
Ah!

77
00:10:46,390 --> 00:10:49,200
Sorry for talking down to you from up here.

78
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:51,720
Old man, what's your name?

79
00:10:53,070 --> 00:10:55,000
It's Sverkel.

80
00:10:56,210 --> 00:10:59,860
Go on. Return to your home.

81
00:11:01,300 --> 00:11:04,580
Thank you, Mister Sverkel.

82
00:11:11,910 --> 00:11:13,170
Thorfinn...

83
00:11:14,820 --> 00:11:16,260
And Einar.

84
00:11:16,710 --> 00:11:20,970
I can't thank you enough.

85
00:11:22,230 --> 00:11:24,780
This is reckless, Arnheid.

86
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:28,460
Gardar is already...

87
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:36,790
It's fine.

88
00:11:42,590 --> 00:11:44,340
Please send us off.

89
00:12:32,030 --> 00:12:33,700
I feel cold...

90
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:39,030
Cold to my core.

91
00:12:52,660 --> 00:12:53,970
How miserable.

92
00:12:55,670 --> 00:13:00,970
Such unfortunate men, abandoned by the gods.

93
00:14:12,750 --> 00:14:14,360
You...

94
00:14:16,550 --> 00:14:19,380
You are my new pride.

95
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:22,040
Hjalti...

96
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:25,220
Hjalti, son of Gardar.

97
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:29,210
Father shall fight for you.

98
00:14:30,110 --> 00:14:32,980
For honor, so you can be proud of him.

99
00:14:33,950 --> 00:14:37,100
For wealth that will someday be yours.

100
00:15:39,660 --> 00:15:40,980
Wait!

101
00:17:02,050 --> 00:17:05,940
For honor and wealth...

102
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:10,250
Gardar?

103
00:17:17,620 --> 00:17:22,100
How old is Hjalti now?

104
00:17:23,780 --> 00:17:27,000
Eight? Nine?

105
00:17:31,190 --> 00:17:32,490
He's six.

106
00:17:33,450 --> 00:17:37,060
Ah, forgive me.

107
00:17:37,570 --> 00:17:41,570
I lost track of time since being enslaved.

108
00:17:43,140 --> 00:17:48,050
Six. I see. That's a shame.

109
00:17:49,060 --> 00:17:52,590
I missed his cute years.

110
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:57,380
He was still only one when I last saw him.

111
00:17:59,950 --> 00:18:06,390
Good grief. He's probably forgotten about us.

112
00:18:09,970 --> 00:18:16,100
He's my son. He's surely
grown into a prankster.

113
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:19,740
I bet he lights horses' tails on fire.

114
00:18:21,510 --> 00:18:25,490
You did that as a child?

115
00:18:26,030 --> 00:18:29,800
Yeah. I got in a lot of
trouble with my father.

116
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:42,500
Once he's old enough, he'll probably say
he wants to go adventuring.

117
00:18:43,010 --> 00:18:44,630
All boys do.

118
00:18:49,970 --> 00:18:53,020
But I won't allow it.

119
00:19:08,510 --> 00:19:09,610
Gardar.

120
00:19:25,730 --> 00:19:31,330
I'm all right. I'm just a little tired.

121
00:19:33,520 --> 00:19:35,350
Let me rest.

122
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:19,750
We're really doing this?

123
00:20:19,750 --> 00:20:22,860
Yeah. We've made up our minds.

124
00:20:22,860 --> 00:20:26,840
The villagers' lives will be easier
if we acquire iron.

125
00:20:26,840 --> 00:20:28,360
So will your family's.

126
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:36,110
Fine. Let's go.

127
00:20:36,110 --> 00:20:36,670
All right.

128
00:20:39,190 --> 00:20:41,770
Everyone's already gathered in the square.

129
00:20:41,770 --> 00:20:43,380
Hurry.

130
00:21:08,870 --> 00:21:10,450
Arnheid...

131
00:21:12,640 --> 00:21:14,070
Hjalti...

132
00:21:17,270 --> 00:21:27,270
I'll never leave your sides again.

133
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:25,400
I'm home.

134
00:23:38,290 --> 00:23:39,510
Welcome home.

135
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:47,350
Welcome home, Gardar.

136
00:25:37,260 --> 00:25:40,220
The First Method

137
00:25:37,750 --> 00:25:39,480
"The First Method."
